# max_parser_depth caps recursive descent, which is what keeps one
# deeply nested expression off a client's wire from exhausting the
# parser's C stack on a device with no memory protection.
#
# A tight override of 5 keeps the fixture compact; a real deployment
# sets something like 256.

## mode: repl

@budget-depth=5

> {"id":12,"op":"eval","code":"(((((((1)))))))"}
< "id":12 | "kind":"error" | "code":"budget_depth"
< "id":12 | "kind":"done"
